{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115696",
      "title": "Working with Template Variables",
      "lectureOrder": 129,
      "videoOrder": 123,
      "sourceHash": "642a0dce3fd6fc5199a7db7f49fddec590331721b32420ff1d83441276550f54",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 3.42,
          "en": "So how can we get hold of the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.42,
          "end": 7.863,
          "en": "that were entered by the user into input and textarea?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.73,
          "end": 12.54,
          "en": "Well, there are different ways of getting hold.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.54,
          "end": 16.89,
          "en": "One way would be to use two-way binding with ngModel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.89,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "And you did learn about that earlier before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "and I'll get back to that in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 26.34,
          "en": "But for the moment, I wanna show you an alternative approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 30.54,
          "en": "because this section here is about diving deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.54,
          "end": 33.93,
          "en": "into Angular and working with templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.93,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "and the user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 38.85,
          "en": "And therefore, I wanna show you an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "of extracting the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "that have been entered into those inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 45.72,
          "en": "when they are submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 49.44,
          "en": "And one alternative way of getting hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.44,
          "end": 52.26,
          "en": "of the entire element actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.26,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "and therefore, also if we want to of the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 60.15,
          "en": "that has been entered here is to store that element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.15,
          "end": 62.91,
          "en": "or a reference to that element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.91,
          "end": 66.18,
          "en": "in a so-called template variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.18,
          "end": 68.94,
          "en": "which is a feature offered by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.94,
          "end": 71.88,
          "en": "not a standard browser feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.88,
          "end": 75.36,
          "en": "And you do store an element in a template variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.36,
          "end": 79.02,
          "en": "by adding a special attribute to that element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.02,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "an attribute that starts with a hashtag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "That's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 87.18299999999999,
          "en": "And then any name of your choice, like titleInput,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.11,
          "end": 89.43,
          "en": "but this is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.43,
          "end": 92.343,
          "en": "The hashtag at the beginning is important though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.05,
          "end": 97.74000000000001,
          "en": "This creates a template variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.74000000000001,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "and that's a Angular feature where the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 103.14,
          "en": "to which this variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.14,
          "end": 105.9,
          "en": "this special attribute here is added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.9,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "is stored in that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 111.69,
          "en": "And that variable is now available anywhere here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.69,
          "end": 115.62,
          "en": "in that template, which means we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.62,
          "end": 120.62,
          "en": "pass it to onSubmit without the hashtag here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 125.28,
          "en": "The hashtag is just important to create that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.28,
          "end": 128.31,
          "en": "So you use it when you add it on the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.31,
          "end": 130.53,
          "en": "that should be stored in the variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.53,
          "end": 134.25,
          "en": "If you then refer to that element anywhere in your template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.25,
          "end": 137.13,
          "en": "you use the variable name without the hashtag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.13,
          "end": 138.633,
          "en": "like I'm doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "So with that, this input element will be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "as an argument to onSubmit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 147.81,
          "en": "So to get a better understanding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.81,
          "end": 152.13,
          "en": "of what exactly is stored in that titleInput thing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.13,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "let's go to onSubmit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 158.97,
          "en": "and there, let's accept an argument, a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.97,
          "end": 163.683,
          "en": "which I'll name, titleElement, the name is up to you though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.67000000000002,
          "end": 167.57999999999998,
          "en": "and let's set a type for this parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.57999999999998,
          "end": 170.31,
          "en": "because since we're using TypeScript, we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.31,
          "end": 175.31,
          "en": "to let TypeScript know which kind of value will be received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.35,
          "end": 177.66,
          "en": "through that parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.66,
          "end": 179.34,
          "en": "Hence you must add a colon here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.34,
          "end": 183.24,
          "en": "and then tell TypeScript which type of element that is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "And we can see which type of element it is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 187.29,
          "en": "if we go back to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.29,
          "end": 189.153,
          "en": "and we hover over titleInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.35,
          "end": 193.203,
          "en": "Here you see that it's of type HTMLInputElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 199.41,
          "en": "which is a type that's built into TypeScript in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 203.22,
          "en": "It is a type that describes the underlying DOM object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.22,
          "end": 205.82999999999998,
          "en": "of such an input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.82999999999998,
          "end": 208.503,
          "en": "So the type here should also be HTMLInputElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.43,
          "end": 211.23,
          "en": "written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.23,
          "end": 213.18,
          "en": "Make sure you get the casing right,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 214.983,
          "en": "otherwise you'll get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 216.45,
          "end": 218.1,
          "en": "Well, and with that, we can,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.1,
          "end": 221.04,
          "en": "of course, lock this titleElement here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.04,
          "end": 222.963,
          "en": "to see what's inside it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.4,
          "end": 225.66,
          "en": "So if I do all that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.66,
          "end": 229.98,
          "en": "and I save it all, if I again click submit here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.98,
          "end": 234.98,
          "en": "you will see that the input here is logged like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 235.2,
          "end": 237.18,
          "en": "Now, that's a bit hard to analyze",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.18,
          "end": 239.34,
          "en": "because for convenience reasons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 243.3,
          "en": "the Chrome dev tools actually output that element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.3,
          "end": 245.76,
          "en": "as an HTML element here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.76,
          "end": 250.59,
          "en": "But actually what we get is an object, a JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.59,
          "end": 254.52,
          "en": "and the Chrome dev tools will output it as an object instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.52,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "of giving you that convenience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 259.44,
          "en": "if you use console.dir instead of console.log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.44,
          "end": 262.173,
          "en": "which is a different way of logging it to the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.79,
          "end": 266.34,
          "en": "With that used, if you now click submit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.34,
          "end": 267.78,
          "en": "you will get an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 267.78,
          "end": 269.22,
          "en": "which you can expand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 269.22,
          "end": 271.62,
          "en": "and you then see all the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.62,
          "end": 274.17,
          "en": "that exist on this object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 274.17,
          "end": 277.77,
          "en": "And these are all default properties that are set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.77,
          "end": 279.9,
          "en": "and controlled by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.9,
          "end": 284.49,
          "en": "because we're accessing the default DOM object in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.49,
          "end": 288.06,
          "en": "the default object that is created by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.06,
          "end": 291.99,
          "en": "behind the scenes for that input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.99,
          "end": 294.57,
          "en": "So this has nothing to do with TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.57,
          "end": 296.52,
          "en": "nothing to do with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 296.52,
          "end": 298.71,
          "en": "You could get hold of that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 298.71,
          "end": 302.19,
          "en": "with just vanilla JavaScript as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 302.19,
          "end": 303.69,
          "en": "Of course, not by using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.69,
          "end": 306.72,
          "en": "that template variable syntax here though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.72,
          "end": 309.18,
          "en": "that is Angular specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 309.18,
          "end": 311.28,
          "en": "but the object that is yielded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.28,
          "end": 316.2,
          "en": "by this syntax is the standard browser input DOM object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 316.2,
          "end": 318.363,
          "en": "That's just important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 319.26,
          "end": 323.28,
          "en": "And you can learn more about that default object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.28,
          "end": 326.43,
          "en": "and which methods and properties exist on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.43,
          "end": 327.93,
          "en": "and what they're all about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 327.93,
          "end": 331.41,
          "en": "if you, for example, visit the official MDN article",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 331.41,
          "end": 332.613,
          "en": "for HTMLInputElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.81,
          "end": 335.613,
          "en": "You find a link to it attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 336.54,
          "end": 339.6,
          "en": "Now, one piece of data we can extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.6,
          "end": 343.77,
          "en": "from that object is the value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 343.77,
          "end": 348.72,
          "en": "If you scroll down here, you will find a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 348.72,
          "end": 351.78,
          "en": "And that's interesting because if I reload here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 351.78,
          "end": 353.49,
          "en": "and I enter something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.49,
          "end": 358.49,
          "en": "and I click submit, you will see that now if I scroll down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 359.22,
          "end": 361.593,
          "en": "to that value property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 363.48,
          "end": 367.41,
          "en": "the entered text is stored in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 367.41,
          "end": 370.89300000000003,
          "en": "and that would be an alternative way of extracting it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 371.79,
          "end": 376.79,
          "en": "So if I wanted to get the enteredTitle, I could get it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 376.92,
          "end": 380.613,
          "en": "by accessing titleElement.value like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 382.14,
          "end": 387.14,
          "en": "and then I can log the entered title like that, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 392.58,
          "end": 396.87,
          "en": "If I do that and save that all, if I again enter test here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 396.87,
          "end": 400.47,
          "en": "and click submit, you see that is being output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 400.47,
          "end": 402.48,
          "en": "and that would be an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 402.48,
          "end": 404.79,
          "en": "of extracting the entered value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 404.79,
          "end": 407.52,
          "en": "Is it better than using two-way binding?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 407.52,
          "end": 410.43,
          "en": "Not necessarily, though it might be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 410.43,
          "end": 413.52,
          "en": "because it does not update some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 413.52,
          "end": 415.74,
          "en": "on every keystroke behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 415.74,
          "end": 419.46,
          "en": "But most importantly, it's simply an alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 419.46,
          "end": 422.25,
          "en": "an alternative you'll see in some projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 422.25,
          "end": 424.98,
          "en": "and therefore, an alternative you should be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 424.98,
          "end": 428.25,
          "en": "because, of course, this is an absolutely fine way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 428.25,
          "end": 431.223,
          "en": "of getting hold of the entered input value.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
